  "rationale": "Direct-match candidates for breast carcinoma are present (many models with trait_efo = breast carcinoma). Among the visible direct breast-cancer (non-subtype) models, PGS000007 stands out for endpoint alignment (trait_reported: Breast cancer; phenotyping_reported: Breast Cancer (personal history)) and substantially stronger reported discrimination than other direct matches in context (full_model AUROC 0.78 with only basic covariates age, sex). Competing direct-match options include PGS000332 (incident breast cancer; C-index 0.75 but with a broader clinical/behavioral covariate set including family history, BMI, smoking, etc.), PGS000015 (AUROC 0.69), and PGS000004 (AUROC 0.6573) as well as several benchmarking/repository scores with lower AUROCs (~0.55–0.65). Main limitation: PGS000007 reports only a full-model AUROC (no explicit PRS-only AUROC/R2), and its phenotype is ‘personal history’ rather than incident-only diagnosis, so comparability to pure PRS performance remains uncertain; thus confidence is moderate rather than high."
