  "best_model_id": "PGS000766",
  "confidence": "Moderate",
  "rationale": "Multiple direct-match melanoma PRS candidates are present (e.g., PGS000079, PGS000118, PGS000732, PGS000743, PGS000766, PGS002246/PGS002247, PGS003430, PGS004886, PGS005208). The strongest endpoint-aligned, disease-focused option in the provided set is PGS000766: it targets incident cutaneous melanoma, is developed across many melanoma-relevant cohorts (multi-cohort, disease-focused context), and reports a time-to-event discrimination metric (C-index 0.643) plus an HR per SD of 1.46 (moderate PRS effect). Competing models show limitations in the visible evidence: several report only full-model AUROC without PRS-only metrics and with heavy non-genetic covariate packages (e.g., PGS000743 full-model AUROC 0.74 includes extensive traditional risk factors), while UKB pan-trait/framework-style models (e.g., PGS001304 snpnet) are penalized by the framework/portability context despite having some PRS-only metrics. Confidence is not high because (i) the context includes many additional melanoma models not fully inspectable here (total_found=103) and (ii) most candidates lack clean PRS-only AUROC/R2, making cross-study performance comparisons uncertain."
}

