  "rationale": "Multiple direct-match melanoma PRS candidates are present (e.g., PGS000079/PGS000118/PGS000732/PGS000743/PGS000766/PGS002246/PGS002247/PGS003430/PGS004886/PGS005208). Prioritizing endpoint fidelity and comparable reported performance, PGS002247 is a direct-match for melanoma with an explicitly aligned endpoint (“Incident invasive melanoma”), European evaluation ancestry, and it reports performance including AUROC=0.691 and an R² estimate of 0.072. Among the incident invasive melanoma cluster, it is slightly better supported than the close alternative PGS002246 (AUROC=0.688; R²=0.07). Other candidates either (i) primarily report full-model metrics with potentially heavier clinical covariates (e.g., PGS000743 includes many traditional risk factors), (ii) target narrower/special populations (e.g., familial melanoma, childhood cancer survivors) or different endpoints (e.g., second primary melanoma), or (iii) are framework/portability-style scores (e.g., UKB snpnet). Limitation: the context does not provide PRS-only (no-covariate) AUROC/R² for most candidates, and the incremental PRS contribution vs covariates is not consistently reported, so confidence is moderated despite PGS002247 being the clearest endpoint-faithful, performance-supported option in the provided set."
}

