  "rationale": "Direct-match asthma PRS candidates are abundant (66). The best-supported option in the visible metadata is PGS002727 because it targets a closely aligned endpoint for the asthma concept (phenotyping_reported: pediatric asthma), uses a genome-wide shrinkage method (PRS-CS; 985,837 variants), and provides PRS-relevant validation evidence including a strong per-SD effect size (OR=1.57, 95% CI 1.55–1.60) and an AUROC reported for a full model (0.66, 95% CI 0.65–0.67). Competing candidates either come from pan-trait/framework or portability-style studies (e.g., UKB ‘813 traits’ snpnet scores; UKB ‘Portability of 245 polygenic scores’), report only full-model metrics or partial correlations without clear PRS-only discrimination, or have endpoint shifts (incident-only, time-to-event, or childhood-only) without similarly strong per-SD effect sizes. Limitation: PGS002727’s endpoint is pediatric asthma (not fully generic asthma), its covariates are listed as unknown, and most candidates lack directly comparable PRS-only AUROC/R², so the choice is not definitively high-confidence despite being the most coherent, PRS-informative evidence package among those shown."
}

