  "rationale": "Multiple direct-match asthma PRS candidates are present. PGS002727 is directly aligned to the target disease concept (trait_efo=asthma; phenotyping_reported=\"Pediatric asthma\") and provides comparatively strong, PRS-informative performance evidence including an OR per SD of 1.57 (95% CI 1.55–1.60) and AUROC=0.66, with very large validation (n=391,820) and multi-ancestry evaluation. Its method (PRS-CS; ~985k variants) is a genome-wide shrinkage approach consistent with stronger structural expectations for polygenic traits. Main limitation: endpoint specificity is pediatric asthma (not generic all-age asthma) and covariates are listed as unknown, which lowers certainty versus adult/general asthma endpoints (e.g., UKB doctor-diagnosed asthma scores) that have cleaner covariate reporting but do not show comparably strong per-SD effect-size evidence in the provided metadata."
