  "confidence": "Moderate",
  "rationale": "Direct-match candidates are present, including multiple scores whose trait_efo is exactly \"ovarian neoplasm\" (PGS000544–PGS000564) and several very close ovarian-cancer endpoints (e.g., ovarian carcinoma). Among the exact-EFO matches, PGS000550 has the strongest visible discrimination/effect evidence as a genome-wide shrinkage model (PRS-CS; 1,115,189 variants) with the highest (or tied-highest) full-model AUROC in that exact-label family (0.568) and the largest reported per-SD OR (1.286, 95% CI 1.169–1.414) compared with other ovarian-neoplasm siblings (generally AUROC ~0.52–0.56 and lower ORs). Main limitation: the reported AUROC is a full-model metric (age/sex/batch/PC adjustment) rather than a PGS-only metric, and several near-synonymous ovarian-carcinoma models show higher full-model AUROCs in much larger cohorts but are not exact ovarian-neoplasm EFO matches; this keeps confidence from being High."
